@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### localhost 3k
GET {{baseUrl}}

### pokemons - listar todos
GET {{baseUrl}}/pokemon

### pokemons - listar disponibles
GET {{baseUrl}}/pokemon/available

### pokemons - listar vendidos
GET {{baseUrl}}/pokemon/sold

### pokemons - obtener uno por id
GET {{baseUrl}}/pokemon/1

### pokemons - obtener uno inexistente (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pokemon/999

### pokemons - crear
POST {{baseUrl}}/pokemon
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bulbasaur",
  "level": 8,
  "price": 0.55
}

### pokemons - actualizar (parcial)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pokemon/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "level": 10
}

### pokemons - actualizar inexistente (404)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/pokemon/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "level": 10
}

### pokemons - comprar
POST {{baseUrl}}/pokemon/1/buy

### pokemons - comprar ya vendido (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/pokemon/1/buy

### sales - crear checkout (devuelve { sale, url }; abrir la url para pagar en Stripe)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sale
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client": "Ash Ketchum",
  "address": "Pallet Town 1",
  "productId": 1
}

### sales - listar
GET {{baseUrl}}/sale

### sales - obtener una por id
GET {{baseUrl}}/sale/1

### sales - actualizar cliente/direccion (precio y status no se pueden tocar)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/sale/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "address": "Viridian City 2"
}

### sales - borrar (409 si ya esta COMPLETED)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sale/1

### sales - paginas de retorno de Stripe (redirigen a /app)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sale/success?session_id=cs_test_123

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/sale/cancel

### sales - webhook sin firma (400). El real lo envia Stripe: stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/sale/webhook
POST {{baseUrl}}/sale/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{}
